<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Berthold VII, Count of Henneberg-Schleusingen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1272">1272</a>–<a href="/years/1340">1340</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Berthold the Wise</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Berthold VII (1272–1340), called the Wise, was Count of Henneberg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schleusingen">Schleusingen</a>, raised to the rank of princely count in 1310. He became one of the closest advisers of Emperor Louis IV the Bavarian, serving him as diplomat and as regent in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> for the emperor's young son Louis. He greatly enlarged the family's lands between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franconia">Franconia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a>.</p></div>
